  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin circular coin of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;is initially in a horizontal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>-plane. The coin is tossed vertically&nbsp;up (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></math> direction) by applying an impulse of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;from its center. The coin spins&nbsp;about its diameter and moves along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></math> direction. By the time the coin reaches back to its initial position, it&nbsp;completes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> rotations. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is _____.</p><p>[Given: The acceleration due to gravity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0002_09a2050e6252.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 199px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "30",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>By impulse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> momentum theorem:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>J</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;Total time of journey&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Also, by angular impulse<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> momentum theorem:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mstyle><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;Number of rotations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>150</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}